course: dictionary
lesson: 5680
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Lobby» is one of them. Its most common meaning is the large hall just inside the front door of a hotel, cinema or office building, where you wait before going further in.
explain: Read the words around the word to choose the right meaning. «Jayden's squad got a player who screamed every time they lost, so they left the lobby and played with their real friends instead.» Here the lobby is a waiting place before a game starts, and players can leave it to join a different game. The clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Lobby» can also be a verb. To lobby means to try to persuade people in charge, such as politicians or your head teacher, to do something. «The children wanted a longer lunch break, so they decided to lobby the head teacher.» Check it by swapping in your meaning: "they decided to try to persuade the head teacher" still makes sense.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check the clues in the sentence.
fact: A lobby is a large hall or entrance area, such as the one in a hotel, theatre, flats or office building.
fact: A lobby group is a group of people who try to get politicians to make or change laws for their cause.
fact: As a verb, «lobby» means to try to persuade politicians or people in charge to do something.
fact: In the UK, a lobby in Parliament is a hall where members of the public can meet MPs.
exercise: «Jayden's squad got a player who screamed every time they lost, so they left the lobby and played with their real friends instead.» What is the lobby in this sentence? | *A waiting area where players gather before a game starts | A bus stop outside a school | A cooking pot used in a kitchen | A group of politicians who make laws
exercise: «The children wanted a longer lunch break, so they decided to lobby the head teacher.» What does lobby mean here? | Eat a big snack | *Try to persuade the head teacher to agree | Paint a sign for the playground | Sleep in the head teacher's office
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the place where people wait in a hotel. The hotel lobby was full of people checking in. | checking | people | *lobby | hotel
test: A lobby group is a group that… | Cleans the lobby of a cinema every day | *Tries to get politicians to make or change laws for their cause | Plays games together on a school trip | Cooks lunch for a hotel
test: «The hotel lobby was cool and quiet.» What does lobby mean in this sentence? | A loud argument | A politician's speech | *The large entrance hall just inside the front door | A small room upstairs
exam: Which sentence uses lobby as a verb? | I waited in the lobby for my friend | The lobby group met on Tuesday | *We will lobby the council to build a new skate park | The lobby was painted bright blue
